          "perks": [],
          "description": "The iron logging axe is a power level 4 logging axe that can be crafted at a blacksmith's bench. The iron logging axe is able to cut the same kinds of trees as the previous tiers, along with blightwood roots and bloodwood sap. Deals 30 damage when felling applicable trees, and 45 when overhead chopping to split them.\n\n(Journal)\nWhile it might be cheaper to use bronze, there are some times when sheer power is necessary. For those times, a lumberjack need look no further than the glittering might of an iron axe’s blade. The mightiest of Ghornfell trees falls before its onslaught, and none in that region may stand against its might.\n\nIron was so powerful, that it created a problem in Brynmoor. The population craved the metal so desperately that they mined the region almost dry. This let to infighting, small civil skirmishes and the white knights of the Blue Flame Keep, needed to be brought in to keep the peace.\n\nIt is said that where iron goes, blood soon follows."
