          "description": "Poisoned bronze arrows are bronze arrows that are coated with weapon poison. Targets that are hit by a poisoned bronze arrow will be inflicted with the Poison debuff, damaging the enemy by 5% of their max health for six seconds. Like other poisoned arrows, the icon will have a Poison icon placed on the top right of the arrow to distinguish itself from regular arrows.\n\n(Journal)\nThe Wild Knights were not above poison, any edge in a battle was worth having. Poison meant that you could take down a dangerous beast, even if your initial shot wasn’t a mortal one.\n\nThe druids among the order felt little concern over its use either, after all nature is filled with wielders of poison and so the Wild Knight archers were simply emulating nature’s tools."
